    "source": "~/BGit/all/film/marketing/ACT3_marketing_Home/act3/rows/row_14_labor_saved/10",
    "html": "<section class=\"r14v10-row\" aria-labelledby=\"r14v10-title\">\n  <div class=\"r14v10-wrap\">\n    <div class=\"r14v10-top\">\n      <div class=\"r14v10-copy\">\n        <p class=\"r14v10-eyebrow\">Months of labor, saved</p>\n        <h2 class=\"r14v10-title\" id=\"r14v10-title\">Your evenings stay yours.</h2>\n        <p class=\"r14v10-body\">ACT 3 does the heavy production work. It casts, builds the sets, plans every shot, writes every prompt and runs the renders in the background. You spend the day on the story, close the laptop for dinner, and the film keeps moving.</p>\n      </div>\n      <figure class=\"r14v10-photo\">\n        <img src=\"/v4/row_14/v/evening.jpg\" width=\"1600\" height=\"893\" loading=\"lazy\"\n             alt=\"Evening at home: a filmmaker closes her laptop, the beach film still on the screen, and turns smiling toward her family setting the dinner table.\">\n        <figcaption class=\"r14v10-cap\">18:30. The beach scene can wait for morning.</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"r14v10-day\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"An example day on Low Tide\">\n      <div class=\"r14v10-rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"r14v10-now\"></span></div>\n      <ol class=\"r14v10-marks\">\n        <li class=\"r14v10-mark r14v10-you\"><span class=\"r14v10-time\">09:00</span><span class=\"r14v10-who\">You</span><span class=\"r14v10-what\">Rewrite Scene 4</span></li>\n        <li class=\"r14v10-mark r14v10-act3\"><span class=\"r14v10-time\">11:30</span><span class=\"r14v10-who\">ACT 3</span><span class=\"r14v10-what\">Shots, prompts and first frames for the scene</span></li>\n        <li class=\"r14v10-mark r14v10-you\"><span class=\"r14v10-time\">14:00</span><span class=\"r14v10-who\">You</span><span class=\"r14v10-what\">Approve the storyboards</span></li>\n        <li class=\"r14v10-mark r14v10-act3\"><span class=\"r14v10-time\">15:00</span><span class=\"r14v10-who\">ACT 3</span><span class=\"r14v10-what\">Renders queued, running in the background</span></li>\n        <li class=\"r14v10-mark r14v10-you r14v10-dinner\"><span class=\"r14v10-time\">18:30</span><span class=\"r14v10-who\">You</span><span class=\"r14v10-what\">Dinner. Laptop closed.</span></li>\n        <li class=\"r14v10-mark r14v10-you\"><span class=\"r14v10-time\">08:00</span><span class=\"r14v10-who\">You</span><span class=\"r14v10-what\">Watch the scene, give notes</span></li>\n      </ol>\n      <p class=\"r14v10-note\">An example day on <em>Low Tide</em>. Pre-production that once took 80&ndash;200 hours takes about 2 in ACT 3.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>",
